2. Account Registration and Operating Requirements
The NextGen ReefTech mobile application requires users to create an account to access application-based functionality.
Internet access is required to download the App and complete initial account registration. Once registered, users may access supported lighting control features through Bluetooth without an active internet connection or Wi-Fi configuration.
Wi-Fi connectivity is optional and enables additional features, including cloud synchronization and automatic system diagnostic reporting.
2.1 Manual Operation Without an Account
Users who do not wish to create an account or use the App may operate their ReefEvolve lighting system through three physical potentiometers integrated into the lighting fixture.
These controls provide manual adjustment of:
• Blues: The blue lighting group;
• Whites: The white lighting group; and
• Shimmer: The shimmer lighting group.
Manual operation does not require account registration, the App, Wi-Fi connectivity, or internet access.
However, users operating exclusively through the physical controls will not have access to App-specific features, including programmable lighting schedules, individual channel control, preview functions, acclimation modes, and other supported software-based features.
Manual operation through the physical potentiometers does not itself transmit personal information or operational data to NextGen ReefTech servers.
2.2 Bluetooth Operation
Registered users may operate their ReefEvolve lighting system through Bluetooth without enabling Wi-Fi connectivity.
Bluetooth operation supports available App functions, including lighting schedules, individual channel adjustments, preview functions, acclimation modes, and other supported features.
Lighting commands are communicated locally between the mobile device and ReefEvolve lighting system.
Lighting schedules and configurations are stored locally on the mobile device and lighting system.
Automatic ReefEvolve system diagnostic reporting and cloud synchronization are not enabled during Bluetooth-only operation.
Account registration, authentication, and certain third-party App services may involve separate information processing, as described in this Privacy Policy.
2.3 Wi-Fi and Cloud-Connected Operation
Registered users may optionally establish Wi-Fi connectivity to access supported cloud-connected functionality.
When Wi-Fi connectivity is enabled:
• Lighting schedules and configurations may be synchronized between the mobile device, ReefEvolve lighting system, and NextGen ReefTech cloud infrastructure;
• Relevant device and operational information may be processed to support cloud services;
• Automatic ReefEvolve system diagnostic reporting is enabled; and
• Cloud-based diagnostic information may be used for technical support, maintenance, security, and product improvement.
Users are not required to enable Wi-Fi connectivity to access supported Bluetooth lighting functions.
