Wi-Fi configuration is optional for App operation.
3.4 Automatic System Diagnostics
Automatic ReefEvolve system diagnostic reporting occurs when a registered user establishes Wi-Fi connectivity and uses supported cloud services.
Depending on the event and available diagnostic capabilities, collected information may include:
• Product and device identifiers;
• Firmware versions;
• System errors and fault codes;
• Connectivity interruptions;
• Software-update results;
• Relevant operating conditions;
• Diagnostic timestamps;
• Technical performance information; and
• Configuration information reasonably necessary to investigate technical problems.
This information may be associated with a registered account or lighting system to facilitate troubleshooting and support.
Automatic ReefEvolve system diagnostic reports are not transmitted to NextGen ReefTech servers during Bluetooth-only operation.
Diagnostic reports are not intended to contain Wi-Fi passwords, authentication secrets, or unrelated personal content.
