5. Local Storage and Cloud Synchronization
ReefEvolve supports local operation and optional cloud-connected operation.
5.1 Local Storage
During Bluetooth-only operation, lighting schedules and configurations are stored on the user's mobile device and ReefEvolve lighting system.
This information is not synchronized with NextGen ReefTech cloud storage unless supported Wi-Fi cloud connectivity is enabled.
5.2 Cloud Storage
When Wi-Fi cloud connectivity is enabled through a registered account, supported schedules and configurations are stored on the mobile device, ReefEvolve lighting system, and NextGen ReefTech cloud infrastructure.
Cloud-stored information is processed to provide synchronization and associated connected functionality.
5.3 Removal of Locally Stored Information
Deleting the App may remove locally stored application information, subject to the mobile operating system and applicable backup mechanisms.
Deleting the App does not necessarily erase schedules or configurations retained by the ReefEvolve lighting system.
Users should follow applicable reset procedures before transferring, selling, or disposing of their lighting system.
6. Diagnostic Monitoring and Troubleshooting Limitations
Wi-Fi connectivity is optional for normal App operation but is required for cloud-based diagnostic monitoring.
When a registered user's ReefEvolve lighting system is connected through Wi-Fi, relevant diagnostic information may be automatically transmitted to NextGen ReefTech servers.
This information assists with:
• Identifying technical problems;
• Investigating reported malfunctions;
• Reviewing system errors;
• Evaluating connectivity interruptions;
• Understanding operating conditions preceding an incident; and
• Improving product reliability.
Important Diagnostic Limitation
Users who choose Bluetooth-only operation may have limited historical diagnostic information available to NextGen ReefTech.
Because automatic cloud-based diagnostic reporting is not enabled during Bluetooth-only operation, NextGen ReefTech may be unable to review the operational events preceding a reported malfunction.
Establishing Wi-Fi connectivity after an incident does not guarantee that earlier diagnostic information will be available.
Consequently, the Company may be unable to determine the precise cause of certain reported issues when relevant historical records were not previously collected.
These limitations do not eliminate applicable warranty rights, statutory protections, or legal obligations.
7. Remote Access and Administrative Control
NextGen ReefTech personnel do not have remote administrative access to operate or control customers' ReefEvolve lighting systems.
Company personnel cannot independently change a customer's lighting schedules, adjust lighting intensity, or remotely operate the lighting system through an administrative console.
NextGen ReefTech may maintain administrative tools for cloud services, diagnostic information, software maintenance, and authorized firmware distribution.
These capabilities do not grant Company personnel remote control over customer lighting operations.
